<!-- ============ 7 · REFLECTION ============ -->
<section class="chapter" id="reflection" aria-labelledby="h-reflection">
  <header class="chapter-head">
    <span class="no">06</span>
    <h2 id="h-reflection">Reflection</h2>
  </header>
  <div class="chapter-body">
    <ol class="learned" data-reveal>
      <li><span class="n">01</span><p><strong>Data analysis often becomes a data-engineering problem first.</strong> Much of the work was cleaning, matching, reshaping, and validating information from different sources.</p></li>
      <li><span class="n">02</span><p><strong>Gower distance handles mixed data.</strong> It gave me a way to compare observations containing both numeric and categorical features.</p></li>
      <li><span class="n">03</span><p><strong>A project can evolve when the first question leads to a more interesting one.</strong> What started as a focused revenue analysis became an exploration of how to quantify similarity across anime.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="takeaway" data-reveal>
      <h3>From a focused Bayesian analysis to a broader research workflow.</h3>
      <ol class="flow is-plain">
        <li>Ask about Miyazaki's impact</li><li>Build &amp; clean the data</li><li>Model similarity</li><li>Visualize</li><li>Explore influence</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

